From d93e73a7777572252e83cf1184c0927c39ded4f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:38:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2043/2064] RendererDRMPRIME: scan out an eye per plane from
 its own buffer

Stereoscopic playback already puts an eye on each of two DRM planes, but both
planes read one framebuffer and take half of it each. A plane's source and
destination rectangles are independent, so there is nothing stopping the two from
reading different buffers instead - which is what a decoder that keeps the views
apart will hand over.

The bridge tracked one buffer and one framebuffer per generation. Make it a set:
the views of a picture are acquired and released together and leave the screen
together, so the early-release accounting stays one decision a frame, taken over
the pair. PrepareBuffer() splits into FramebufferFor(), which is per buffer, and
Present(), which takes up a whole generation at once - the framebuffers have to be
in hand before the reap, or the protection set would not cover the pair that is
about to go on screen. UpdateVideoPlane() re-arms both planes.

Which eye a plane shows now decides which buffer it gets, and that is the cadence's
to say: for a right_left source the display's first half wants the second view.
SetStereoPlaneGeometry() already drives the stereo view once per eye to get the
geometry, so it records the answer while it is there. Where the views are packed
both planes get the same buffer and the crop picks the eye as before, so nothing
changes for a natively packed side-by-side or over-under file.

Create() turns the stream down when the views come separately and no second plane
can be had, handing back the reservation the search above it made. There is no
crop that shows two buffers on one plane, so it is better to let a compositing
renderer have the stream than to show one eye twice; the factory tries drm_prime
before drm_prime_gles, so declining is how that choice is expressed.

The framebuffer cache holds a framebuffer per dma-buf and there are now twice as
many in rotation, so raise its cap - an overflow re-imports the buffer it evicted,
every frame.

(cherry picked from commit a10fa365aedae4589fcaf20879d4597f7ea13398)
